WEBVTT

01:03.313 --> 01:05.982
GENIE, MAKE A WISH

01:11.571 --> 01:13.031
Won't you come with me

01:13.615 --> 01:14.949
to the moment you died?

01:18.787 --> 01:20.288
How could I trust you?

01:22.665 --> 01:25.460
I followed his orders
and bowed before the first human.

01:26.044 --> 01:30.256
Iblis has been my brother for the longest
and my enemy for just as long.

01:32.175 --> 01:34.219
Iblis is trying to kill you,
Ms. Ki Ka-young.

01:34.803 --> 01:36.137
The enemy of an enemy…

01:38.348 --> 01:39.307
is surely a friend?

01:57.325 --> 01:58.409
Piss off.

01:58.952 --> 02:01.121
-Why?
-Your face just now.

02:01.204 --> 02:02.831
You were being deceptive.

02:05.041 --> 02:06.501
What? Did you bite your tongue?

02:08.086 --> 02:10.421
Someone just whacked my master.

02:10.505 --> 02:11.673
Really?

02:11.756 --> 02:14.926
Someone who would beat up Ejllael?
I only know of two.

02:19.806 --> 02:22.267
One of them is occupied, which means…

02:25.103 --> 02:27.397
I have to get to work
early tomorrow, so I'm off.

02:31.192 --> 02:32.360
Good morning, Ms. Ki.

02:34.445 --> 02:35.822
Did something happen?

02:35.905 --> 02:38.158
We're with the police.

02:38.783 --> 02:42.662
Did Ejllael report you for assault?
He is a stickler for protocol.

02:42.745 --> 02:45.290
I think you're the one
who's ratting me out right now.

02:46.666 --> 02:48.376
They're on a missing persons case.

02:48.960 --> 02:53.006
Do you recognize this woman?
This village was her last known location.

02:55.925 --> 02:57.635
I tend to track things by scent.

03:00.680 --> 03:01.764
We haven't seen her.

03:02.265 --> 03:04.017
Could I take a picture of this?

03:04.100 --> 03:04.976
Sure.

03:05.059 --> 03:08.605
Please do get in touch
if anything comes to mind.

03:37.842 --> 03:38.968
BLACK HAIR DYE

03:42.347 --> 03:45.266
That's strange. I was just here last week.

03:45.350 --> 03:47.227
Why'd they request another visit so soon?

03:49.604 --> 03:52.774
Anyone home? Ms. Shin Suk-ja?
It's your water filter technician.

03:55.109 --> 03:56.402
What's that smell?

03:58.238 --> 03:59.906
Apparently, she died alone.

03:59.989 --> 04:01.241
Who found her?

04:01.324 --> 04:03.952
Her kids must not have checked in on her.

04:04.619 --> 04:07.664
Why do you always handle things
in such a complicated manner?

04:08.831 --> 04:11.709
If I am to keep accompanying
those who die alone,

04:11.793 --> 04:13.878
I must adapt to human protocol.

04:13.962 --> 04:16.881
I made every report myself
until about 40 years ago.

04:17.382 --> 04:19.133
I was really busy back then.

04:19.676 --> 04:22.512
I'd listen to the dying's last complaints
and file the reports,

04:22.595 --> 04:23.972
all in heavy clothes.

04:26.057 --> 04:27.225
I can't.

04:27.308 --> 04:29.560
I can't leave my sick girl behind.
I just can't.

04:30.144 --> 04:33.731
Please give me more time
until my granddaughter gets better.

04:33.815 --> 04:34.857
Please.

04:35.358 --> 04:37.277
You don't have to worry about that.

04:37.986 --> 04:38.820
It's not you.

04:39.862 --> 04:40.697
It's her.

04:42.448 --> 04:43.658
No, it can't be!

04:43.741 --> 04:45.702
Then the police started looking for me.

04:45.785 --> 04:47.912
Because death follows me everywhere.

04:48.496 --> 04:50.540
I'm probably still wanted by Interpol.

04:50.623 --> 04:51.541
I see.

04:51.624 --> 04:54.002
Then why were you hit by Ms. Ki Ka-young?

04:55.044 --> 04:57.213
Fail to consider protocol
when convincing her?

05:01.718 --> 05:04.554
The fact that you know
means Iblis already knows too.

05:06.472 --> 05:07.307
Of course.

05:07.390 --> 05:10.143
I hear the talk of the day,
and Sade hears the night's.

05:14.230 --> 05:16.107
Why are you hogging them both?

05:16.190 --> 05:17.650
This is a fight against myself.

05:17.734 --> 05:20.653
Why is an adult doing this
in broad daylight?

05:20.737 --> 05:21.904
Are you a bum?

05:21.988 --> 05:23.364
No, I'm a respectable genie.

05:23.448 --> 05:26.075
And I'm immortal,
so I'm practically an infant.

05:27.368 --> 05:28.703
So I'm older than you?

05:29.287 --> 05:31.372
Hey, infant. Move over.

05:32.040 --> 05:33.833
No wonder Ka-young doesn't like you.

05:38.504 --> 05:39.672
What did you just say?

05:39.756 --> 05:41.883
Sorry for calling you an infant.

05:41.966 --> 05:44.302
Ki Ka-young doesn't like me?

05:44.969 --> 05:47.930
If anyone should dislike anyone, it's me.
Did she tell you that?

05:48.765 --> 05:51.100
Please tell me everything you know,
Mr. Sang-hyeok.

05:51.601 --> 05:52.435
Master.

05:55.521 --> 05:57.982
Ejllael personally went
to the lump of clay's house? Why?

05:58.066 --> 05:59.692
I hear he was being all enchanting,

05:59.776 --> 06:02.362
saying, "Won't you come with me
to the moment you died?"

06:02.445 --> 06:03.529
The moment she died?

06:07.825 --> 06:09.160
That won't be good for me.

06:09.243 --> 06:10.078
And?

06:10.161 --> 06:14.123
When he said that, Master's master
told Ejllael to "piss off" and then just

06:14.207 --> 06:15.291
went for it.

06:16.459 --> 06:18.544
She doesn't give me dinner
if she's in a mood.

06:19.879 --> 06:20.922
I should go check.

06:22.423 --> 06:23.257
Distract the man.

06:24.842 --> 06:25.676
The man?

06:26.594 --> 06:27.595
Ki Ka-young!

06:31.057 --> 06:32.600
Wait, this is my carpet.

06:33.559 --> 06:35.478
Gosh, how could she use it to…

06:40.274 --> 06:42.068
You're wearing Versac…

06:42.777 --> 06:46.364
You're doing this while wearing that?

06:46.989 --> 06:48.116
Ki Ka-young will be mad.

06:48.199 --> 06:52.078
The only way to train my eye for fashion
is to wear stuff like this every day.

06:52.161 --> 06:54.872
Right, I made hamburger steaks.

06:54.956 --> 06:57.333
Leave some for Ka-young.
She'll be home late.

06:57.417 --> 06:59.710
Where did she go? She wasn't at the auto…

07:02.505 --> 07:03.339
Right.

07:04.715 --> 07:06.259
Today's the fourth.

07:26.654 --> 07:27.905
Aren't you curious

07:28.573 --> 07:30.116
about what happened?

07:53.097 --> 07:54.348
You really are doing

07:54.932 --> 07:56.809
your utmost to die, aren't you?

07:57.310 --> 07:58.269
It's not fair.

07:58.352 --> 08:01.564
What exactly was his purpose
in making you and me meet?

08:02.648 --> 08:06.486
Well, based on your actions,
it couldn't have been to make me happy.

08:08.029 --> 08:11.324
I don't know his intentions,
but if you do die, it'll be at my hands.

08:12.241 --> 08:15.119
If you'd like,
we can say that's the reason we met.

08:44.857 --> 08:48.402
Yoo Jeong-hwa hasn't attended class
for over a month.

09:04.460 --> 09:05.795
Which room is this?

09:05.878 --> 09:08.422
Spare me the bullshit about privacy
and hand me the key,

09:08.506 --> 09:09.715
or I'll call the police.

09:10.216 --> 09:13.469
She's my daughter,
and the boy she's with is a minor.

09:18.891 --> 09:20.393
So fucking annoying.

09:20.476 --> 09:22.770
They're fucking terrible. Fucking idiots.

09:22.853 --> 09:24.397
Pull your weight, damn it.

09:25.231 --> 09:26.524
You suck ass too.

09:26.607 --> 09:28.734
I'm doing perfectly well right now.

09:30.945 --> 09:32.572
How long do other people

09:33.239 --> 09:34.949
keep theirs before making it?

09:36.200 --> 09:37.660
The third wish, I mean.

09:41.205 --> 09:44.292
The longest was a guy
who held on to it for 72 years.

09:45.293 --> 09:46.127
Wow.

09:47.670 --> 09:48.921
I get it though.

09:50.089 --> 09:52.842
Caught between the despair
that there's only one left

09:53.426 --> 09:57.179
and the euphoria of knowing
that you still have one,

09:57.763 --> 09:59.348
you don't want to break the spell.

10:02.518 --> 10:03.728
Tell me.

10:04.228 --> 10:05.605
What did he wish for?

10:05.688 --> 10:08.608
Most humans make
their first wish right away,

10:09.108 --> 10:11.736
afraid that their newfound luck
may vanish.

10:12.528 --> 10:14.155
Then they use their second wish,

10:14.238 --> 10:17.325
patching up the first one
they rushed to make,

10:17.950 --> 10:20.828
cursing themselves
for their failure to wish for more.

10:21.537 --> 10:24.832
And then, they live in hell,
clinging to their final wish.

10:24.915 --> 10:28.294
Seeking something greater,
greater, and greater still.

10:29.712 --> 10:32.131
He made his final wish after 72 years.

10:32.632 --> 10:35.301
He wished for me to forget
that he'd already

10:36.052 --> 10:37.303
made two wishes.

10:40.598 --> 10:42.725
He found the greatest thing of all.

10:46.354 --> 10:48.939
Does that work?

10:51.901 --> 10:52.985
What do you think?

10:55.029 --> 10:56.697
If you'd like to know, try it.

11:18.219 --> 11:19.220
Goodness me.

11:21.806 --> 11:24.266
Always put the purse back in its dust bag.

11:24.350 --> 11:25.685
Do not wear on rainy days.

11:25.768 --> 11:28.187
Never ever wear
hot pink Crocs with this outfit.

11:28.270 --> 11:31.148
This outfit goes with
both sneakers and heels.

11:31.232 --> 11:33.984
Keep the shoes simple for a smart look.
And carry this purse.

11:34.068 --> 11:35.653
No fruit knives in the purses.

11:35.736 --> 11:37.196
My goodness, this girl.

11:38.155 --> 11:40.241
I see. So this is how you style them.

11:40.324 --> 11:42.743
Let's see.

11:47.957 --> 11:49.667
Today, I choose you.

12:13.274 --> 12:14.525
4,000 won?

12:15.025 --> 12:16.026
For one of these?

12:16.736 --> 12:19.238
Goodness me,
4,000 won gets you a loaf of bread.

12:20.573 --> 12:24.118
You're wearing designer heels
and a blouse from the latest collection,

12:24.201 --> 12:25.369
yet this is expensive?

12:28.873 --> 12:30.166
You sure are strange.

12:32.001 --> 12:34.128
That I am. Very strange.

12:35.045 --> 12:37.673
Come by my place sometime.
I'll fry you sweet pancakes.

12:37.757 --> 12:38.966
As big as your face.

12:41.218 --> 12:42.261
Just eat one.

12:42.344 --> 12:46.015
The owner here is one of my patients,
and they still need a few more implants.

12:48.184 --> 12:49.685
Then we'd best boost their sales.

12:49.769 --> 12:51.854
Especially if they're
Dr. Choi's patients, no?

12:52.772 --> 12:54.190
All right, let's see.

12:58.861 --> 12:59.904
Too sweet.

13:00.905 --> 13:02.239
Two would be pushing it.

13:02.740 --> 13:04.658
An old-fashioned palate

13:04.742 --> 13:07.244
and an ultra-smooth home invite.

13:08.579 --> 13:10.998
What on earth is this lady's deal?

13:15.711 --> 13:16.629
My deal?

13:17.546 --> 13:20.007
I'm a woman
whose life was a teeny bit difficult

13:20.090 --> 13:22.718
but has recently become
a teeny bit more fun.

13:27.389 --> 13:28.307
Go on. Try it.

13:32.102 --> 13:33.938
Something's definitely off.

13:34.522 --> 13:38.275
Pan-geum may be having
the time of her life in Hawaii,

13:38.359 --> 13:41.028
but there's no way
she wouldn't be in touch for this long.

13:41.111 --> 13:43.823
Some crazy crap is going down.
I just know it.

13:43.906 --> 13:44.865
Right?

13:45.658 --> 13:49.245
It's one thing not to call us,
but she could at least answer our calls.

13:49.829 --> 13:54.208
And it's odd that the moment she left,
a total stranger moved in.

13:55.209 --> 13:59.296
Just now, I saw that young woman
giggling away over cookies with Dr. Choi.

13:59.380 --> 14:02.800
The other night,
I actually saw that girl and Ka-young

14:02.883 --> 14:05.219
digging up Pan-geum's chili field.

14:05.302 --> 14:07.179
I wonder what that was about.

14:07.263 --> 14:09.682
The chili field? Goodness gracious.

14:09.765 --> 14:12.810
Ka-young finally went and did it.

14:13.352 --> 14:16.230
What if she killed her grandma
and buried her?

14:16.313 --> 14:18.357
-There's no way.
-Come on, Heung-rye.

14:18.440 --> 14:22.027
What do you mean there's no way?
The young bitch must be her accomplice!

14:22.111 --> 14:23.988
What are you waiting for? Call Chang-sik!

14:27.241 --> 14:29.869
She's a guest at our house
for a six-month countryside stay.

14:29.952 --> 14:30.911
Cut the crap.

14:30.995 --> 14:35.082
If she's only staying for six months,
why'd she come out of Pan-geum's room?

14:35.165 --> 14:37.459
Now, now. Calm down, everyone.

14:37.543 --> 14:41.213
Our village elders have reasonable
suspicions given the circumstances,

14:41.297 --> 14:43.007
so you'd best answer honestly.

14:43.716 --> 14:46.427
So, where has your grandma gone?

14:47.553 --> 14:50.681
Hawaii. She said it was her dream
when she was young.

14:50.764 --> 14:54.059
She couldn't pick Miss Korea or Hawaii
and regretted missing both.

14:54.560 --> 14:55.519
Hawaii?

14:56.020 --> 14:58.022
"You go to Hawaii." That Hawaii?

14:58.105 --> 14:59.481
All by her merry self?

14:59.565 --> 15:02.151
Why are you still going on about old news?

15:02.234 --> 15:04.028
-She went to Hawaii.
-Yes?

15:04.111 --> 15:06.447
But she's not answering her damn phone!

15:07.281 --> 15:08.574
She went quietly by herself.

15:08.657 --> 15:11.452
See? She just said "she went"!

15:11.535 --> 15:13.203
I told you she killed her!

15:13.871 --> 15:15.539
And this outsider's your accomplice?

15:15.623 --> 15:18.334
Goodness, dearie.
How could you say something so horrific?

15:18.417 --> 15:19.293
Dearie?

15:25.799 --> 15:29.303
Don't you all call each other that
out in the countryside?

15:29.929 --> 15:31.472
That's what they do on TV.

15:32.056 --> 15:35.017
Look at how this minx
is squinting her eyes like this.

15:35.100 --> 15:36.185
Look at her.

15:36.268 --> 15:38.479
Who do you think you're fooling?

15:38.562 --> 15:42.483
You call your grandma right now.
I want to see her with my own eyes!

15:42.566 --> 15:46.904
She's right. Aren't you even worried?
None of us can get hold of her.

15:47.529 --> 15:50.199
What did I tell you? She can't call her.

15:50.282 --> 15:53.661
Just spit it out. You did away
with your grandma, didn't you?

15:53.744 --> 15:54.662
What kind of--

15:55.871 --> 15:56.872
You can't.

16:00.334 --> 16:01.251
Hey.

16:02.211 --> 16:03.712
It's ringing right now.

16:04.588 --> 16:06.256
It'll ring, but she won't answer.

16:06.340 --> 16:07.967
MS. OH PAN-GEUM
CONNECTING

16:11.762 --> 16:13.430
Yes, hello? What is it?

16:14.014 --> 16:17.476
Has something happened?
I'm here in Hawaii.

16:17.559 --> 16:20.646
Right, so you're doing fine.
It's me, Chang-sik.

16:20.729 --> 16:21.939
Say hello, everyone.

16:23.315 --> 16:26.694
Is it night over there?
Gosh, that's so cool.

16:27.277 --> 16:30.406
Just look at the ocean over there.
Amazing, isn't it?

16:30.489 --> 16:32.324
-Hand it over!
-It's a video call!

16:32.408 --> 16:33.283
It's a vid--

16:33.367 --> 16:34.868
You sure are something.

16:34.952 --> 16:38.497
How could you go all by yourself?
I heard you had a spare ticket and all!

16:38.580 --> 16:39.999
Hand it here. Let's all see.

16:40.499 --> 16:43.085
Hey, look at you!
A flower wearing flowers!

16:43.752 --> 16:46.296
Goodness, you're all pretty and glowing.

16:46.922 --> 16:50.634
Pan-geum, why didn't you answer our calls?
And when are you coming back?

16:51.885 --> 16:54.263
I was thinking of staying
for a few more months.

16:54.346 --> 16:56.306
Ka-young is all grown up now,

16:56.390 --> 16:59.309
and my eldest daughter asked me
to come and live with her.

16:59.393 --> 17:01.395
And… Hello?

17:02.104 --> 17:03.355
Hello?

17:03.439 --> 17:06.191
-What's wrong with the connection?
-The reception here is…

17:06.275 --> 17:08.444
-Hello?
-Right, on your way back, I'd love…

17:08.527 --> 17:10.487
Some jojoba oil, but the line cut out.

17:11.071 --> 17:12.865
Either way, you all saw that, right?

17:13.449 --> 17:15.409
We all suspected Ms. Ki for nothing!

17:15.492 --> 17:17.703
At ease. Everyone, disperse!

17:17.786 --> 17:20.330
Honestly. Let's go pick some strawberries!

17:22.082 --> 17:24.126
Why didn't you call her
when we first asked?

17:24.710 --> 17:27.755
You kept talking in circles,
like you were hiding something.

17:27.838 --> 17:29.048
Of course I'd suspect you!

17:29.673 --> 17:30.883
You're not exactly normal.

17:44.104 --> 17:46.440
I thought I'd drop by the village hall,

17:47.524 --> 17:48.942
but I'll lie low from now on.

17:49.860 --> 17:53.155
I caused you such a headache.

18:06.376 --> 18:10.089
Didn't you say you'd come up with
perfectly flawless wishes?

18:11.882 --> 18:12.925
You're grateful as hell?

18:13.717 --> 18:15.219
So it's moments like these.

18:16.136 --> 18:17.554
This is what I get…

18:19.264 --> 18:21.475
for being selfish
and making wishes to Satan.

18:44.790 --> 18:45.916
Hello.

18:47.376 --> 18:50.087
I'm a student studying
how to decipher facial features.

18:50.754 --> 18:52.840
I see you have such a pure soul.

18:55.801 --> 18:57.219
Of course. I would.

18:57.302 --> 18:58.512
I'm a spirit.

18:58.595 --> 19:00.013
But life's giving you trouble?

19:01.431 --> 19:02.474
How did you…

19:04.184 --> 19:07.104
I ought to take pleasure
in my enemy's misfortune, but I don't.

19:07.688 --> 19:11.400
-Why might that be?
-Right. Of course you're unhappy.

19:11.483 --> 19:13.569
I see an ancestor of yours
died on the road.

19:15.028 --> 19:18.699
My ancestor lives on, immortal.
It's my brothers who died far from home.

19:19.992 --> 19:22.369
Almost all of them died
in the war against the angels.

19:24.121 --> 19:26.456
I'm just setting the record straight.

19:29.251 --> 19:30.294
Is that so?

19:30.961 --> 19:32.588
Well, best wishes to you.

19:34.047 --> 19:36.675
Where are you going?
That was just the prologue.

19:37.217 --> 19:39.219
The war lasted 300 years!

19:47.394 --> 19:48.562
Heading home from work?

19:50.939 --> 19:52.149
Ms. Lee?

19:53.609 --> 19:55.694
I'm sorry. Could you repeat that?

19:56.278 --> 19:57.571
I'm deaf,

19:57.654 --> 19:59.323
so my responses are delayed.

19:59.406 --> 20:00.991
I need to read your lips.

20:01.074 --> 20:02.784
Here's your latte.

20:02.868 --> 20:03.827
I had no idea.

20:04.328 --> 20:05.704
Your latte's ready.

20:10.667 --> 20:13.795
I've had a lot of time to practice
because I was born this way.

20:14.713 --> 20:17.007
Because one shouldn't hear
the secrets of heaven.

20:17.591 --> 20:18.508
Excuse me.

20:21.136 --> 20:22.137
What was that?

20:23.180 --> 20:26.642
Sounded like the line, "Lucifer has come
to the school for Satans."

20:27.726 --> 20:30.812
I was born
from a single breath of white smoke,

20:30.896 --> 20:34.775
drawn from a hookah pipe and exhaled
by my master, the angel Ejllael.

20:35.442 --> 20:37.486
When my master made me,
he blocked my ears.

20:37.569 --> 20:41.615
-Lest I trill the secrets of heaven.
-Hey, stop! You've been so nice to me!

20:41.698 --> 20:42.908
Don't get bored with me!

20:43.492 --> 20:44.993
Hey, that's the road!

20:46.411 --> 20:47.621
Oh dear.

20:52.542 --> 20:54.670
All right, you're free to enter now!

21:17.442 --> 21:19.278
I don't think I've seen you here before.

21:20.279 --> 21:21.113
Auntie!

21:21.196 --> 21:23.782
I told you, that's not the bathroom!
Go outside!

21:24.366 --> 21:25.659
So you must all be family.

21:25.742 --> 21:28.120
What do you say?
Do you want in on a round?

21:28.203 --> 21:29.997
But I don't know what that is.

21:30.706 --> 21:31.873
And, most importantly,

21:32.541 --> 21:33.500
I'm broke.

21:34.167 --> 21:36.086
Don't you worry about that.

21:36.169 --> 21:38.213
You'll learn the rules as you play,

21:38.714 --> 21:40.299
and I can lend you some money.

21:40.799 --> 21:43.427
Let's start with a million
with 10% deducted as interest.

21:44.428 --> 21:47.556
Wait, you're just handing me
something so precious?

21:48.932 --> 21:49.766
Thanks.

21:51.518 --> 21:53.520
You must be the leader of this tribe.

21:54.980 --> 21:57.566
Don't get nervous.
I'll approach you slowly.

22:04.990 --> 22:06.742
You've dodged the molestation charges.

22:07.326 --> 22:10.495
So people over there really do
greet each other by touching noses.

22:12.122 --> 22:14.333
You may leave once your guardian arrives.

22:15.334 --> 22:16.251
My guardian?

22:16.752 --> 22:18.837
Wait, can't I just go?

22:18.920 --> 22:21.006
You saw me get beaten up
last time, didn't you?

22:28.430 --> 22:29.264
Molestation?

22:29.765 --> 22:31.850
First you dine and dash. Now molestation?

22:33.560 --> 22:34.394
Wear the clip.

22:35.771 --> 22:36.730
Wear it!

22:38.106 --> 22:39.608
The thing is,

22:39.691 --> 22:41.777
this all came about because…

22:41.860 --> 22:44.112
Seriously, this is so unfair.

22:46.698 --> 22:47.574
Get over here.

22:49.201 --> 22:51.161
Unfair? This is unfair?

22:53.747 --> 22:54.623
Come here.

23:00.587 --> 23:01.671
Get over here.

23:09.346 --> 23:10.180
Two.

23:11.681 --> 23:13.475
I have two left.

23:13.558 --> 23:16.728
Two.

23:17.312 --> 23:19.981
Two.

23:21.900 --> 23:25.987
SA FAMILY GAMJA-TANG

23:28.156 --> 23:30.659
DEPOSIT, KI KA-YOUNG
10,000,000 WON

23:33.328 --> 23:34.454
This is driving me nuts.

23:37.124 --> 23:38.667
CHEONGPUNGHO BANK

23:38.750 --> 23:42.295
The psycho's filthy rich, but her
daily transfer limit is ten million!

23:43.797 --> 23:45.173
That won't do.

23:45.257 --> 23:47.843
If we move it all at once,
they'd investigate immediately.

23:48.468 --> 23:50.137
I'll figure out the rest myself.

23:50.220 --> 23:51.346
Here's my second wish.

23:51.847 --> 23:54.266
Increase Ki Ka-young's transfer limit
to the maximum.

24:08.905 --> 24:11.074
Why would you lock the break room door?

24:11.158 --> 24:13.368
Get out here.
Ki Ka-young is asking for you.

24:24.337 --> 24:27.174
I want to increase my transfer limit
to the maximum.

24:31.136 --> 24:31.970
Sure.

24:33.221 --> 24:34.556
The maximum is 50 million.

24:38.310 --> 24:40.395
Fill out the blanks here and here.

24:40.896 --> 24:42.147
At the bottom here too.

24:59.623 --> 25:02.167
DEPOSIT, KI KA-YOUNG
50,000,000 WON

25:11.343 --> 25:14.930
GU BO-GYEONG, JULY 12, 2024
MADE HER SECOND WISH

25:15.013 --> 25:18.600
INCREASE KI KA-YOUNG'S TRANSFER LIMIT

25:22.020 --> 25:25.941
Every human I've seen loved money the most
and hated losing it most.

25:26.024 --> 25:26.900
Don't you?

25:28.443 --> 25:30.779
Didn't you see me write fast
because I hate it?

25:31.530 --> 25:35.450
But if it's to validate humanity,
losing money would be worthwhile.

25:36.076 --> 25:37.786
It would prove my arrogance.

25:40.872 --> 25:43.875
So stop gloating. I know I'm losing.

25:48.171 --> 25:49.381
Why were you in the water?

25:50.423 --> 25:52.342
Those bubbles were you, right?

25:53.802 --> 25:54.928
I'll go wherever I want.

25:56.763 --> 25:58.890
It's not like you own the ocean.

26:02.352 --> 26:04.771
Is there anything you hate in particular?

26:05.480 --> 26:06.523
Like garlic?

26:07.190 --> 26:08.525
Or a stake?

26:08.608 --> 26:09.651
Or a cross?

26:14.155 --> 26:15.657
I particularly hate you.

26:16.658 --> 26:17.867
Get out.

26:29.087 --> 26:32.090
Hey, Mi-ju. You found your way here.

26:32.173 --> 26:36.386
I'm here, yes, but I'm not sure
a rookie like me could do anything.

26:36.469 --> 26:38.763
I was a complete mess
when I first started.

26:39.264 --> 26:41.057
Played any other sports in the past?

26:41.141 --> 26:42.892
I did a little yoga in the past.

26:42.976 --> 26:45.854
I could get my foot up to my neck
and was pretty flexible.

26:46.771 --> 26:48.356
But I can't go there anymore.

26:48.898 --> 26:50.358
I've been thinking,

26:50.442 --> 26:53.445
I may as well learn something
I could use to protect someone.

26:54.487 --> 26:56.156
Hit this. Show me what you've got.

26:57.616 --> 26:59.784
-Holy smokes!
-Hey, what was that?

27:01.161 --> 27:03.038
You'll get us in big trouble!

27:03.121 --> 27:05.165
Mi-ju, are you loaded?

27:05.248 --> 27:06.916
I think you might have to replace this.

27:07.709 --> 27:10.462
Really? Did they attach it with glue?

27:10.545 --> 27:11.755
I'm joking, of course.

27:13.673 --> 27:14.591
Joking?

27:16.176 --> 27:18.178
Bring it on. Get over here.

27:22.557 --> 27:23.933
About that mansion.

27:24.601 --> 27:26.978
Do you think everyone
in the front yard was family?

27:27.062 --> 27:29.773
Didn't they look
more like guards than family?

27:30.857 --> 27:32.651
No. You can't fool these eyes.

27:33.818 --> 27:35.570
They're not family or guards.

27:36.780 --> 27:39.532
Something is happening
in this peaceful village of mine.

27:40.325 --> 27:41.159
They were…

27:43.536 --> 27:44.371
an army.

27:44.454 --> 27:45.580
-An army?
-An army?

27:45.664 --> 27:47.123
Yes. Military.

27:47.749 --> 27:50.377
GOBLIN STATIONERY

28:01.513 --> 28:03.723
Mister, where did you get that money?

28:04.307 --> 28:06.559
You've always been broke.

28:06.643 --> 28:07.477
Stop right there!

28:07.560 --> 28:08.812
Why?

28:10.021 --> 28:11.147
Empty your pockets.

28:11.856 --> 28:12.691
Why?

28:25.328 --> 28:27.247
Certain dark channels were involved.

28:29.874 --> 28:32.001
All right. It's on me today.

28:32.585 --> 28:34.921
Really? You're being serious, right?

28:42.721 --> 28:46.307
-What's with your arms?
-Certain dark family matters are involved.

28:48.017 --> 28:50.645
By the way, do you want to know a secret?

28:52.397 --> 28:54.357
You have to keep this secret.

28:54.858 --> 28:56.401
Sang-hyeok, run. Quickly!

28:56.484 --> 28:57.986
Get back here, you little shit!

28:58.069 --> 29:00.280
Why take it out on him
when you're short on cash?

29:00.363 --> 29:02.866
That's why I said
get an overdraft account, you bitch!

29:02.949 --> 29:05.702
I can't with my credit score,
you fucking asshole!

29:06.286 --> 29:08.204
I saw an angel.

29:10.623 --> 29:11.750
You did?

29:11.833 --> 29:14.294
I see them occasionally too.
Okay, I'm starting.

29:14.377 --> 29:16.129
I'm being serious.

29:16.212 --> 29:17.797
So I prayed.

29:17.881 --> 29:20.175
I asked them to make
my mom's boyfriend disappear.

29:20.258 --> 29:23.845
That jerk you saw doesn't grant wishes.
You have no idea how selfish he is.

29:23.928 --> 29:25.138
Don't believe me, then.

29:25.722 --> 29:28.099
Seriously, though,
as soon as I'm a bit bigger,

29:28.183 --> 29:30.101
I'd probably be able to beat him up.

29:30.685 --> 29:33.188
But it just takes too long to grow up.

29:40.028 --> 29:41.321
Okay, give me 100 won.

29:41.404 --> 29:43.114
But you have a lot of money now.

29:43.198 --> 29:47.160
I'm saying I'll grant that wish for you.
But nothing in this world is free.

29:47.660 --> 29:51.164
You wouldn't know, but the true
wish specialist is… Woo-hoo! I won!

29:53.708 --> 29:55.043
I'll trust you this once.

29:55.543 --> 29:57.504
I deliberately lost
a 100-won match to you.

29:58.213 --> 29:59.923
What? Wow.

30:01.216 --> 30:02.425
You're worse than Satan.

30:02.509 --> 30:05.136
All right.
It's just until you become an adult.

30:05.220 --> 30:06.846
You're 12 years old right now,

30:07.639 --> 30:11.518
so I'll have them maul him just enough
to keep him bedridden for 7.5 years.

30:22.320 --> 30:24.364
My arms. My legs.

30:26.699 --> 30:28.576
I know this face.

30:31.079 --> 30:31.913
Who are you?

30:32.497 --> 30:34.749
Send help! A man's dying out here!

30:36.334 --> 30:37.168
A man?

30:38.753 --> 30:40.129
I don't see a man here.

30:40.630 --> 30:43.007
You beat a 12-year-old
and call yourself a man?

30:43.091 --> 30:44.759
Even Satan would shed tears…

30:46.135 --> 30:47.303
Good job holding back.

30:49.597 --> 30:50.807
In BC,

30:50.890 --> 30:53.935
I fought for three centuries
to protect my brothers.

30:54.894 --> 30:57.188
Today, in 2024 AD,

30:58.523 --> 31:00.984
I start yet another war
for the sake of a brother.

31:04.696 --> 31:06.823
Sang-hyeok is an enemy,
but he's also a comrade.

31:07.615 --> 31:09.200
And he chose to become my friend.

31:11.035 --> 31:13.288
That is the reason
for your current suffering.

31:20.503 --> 31:22.130
Help me!

31:22.213 --> 31:25.717
Help me! I was wrong. Please!

31:25.800 --> 31:27.051
How unlucky.

31:27.135 --> 31:28.136
Help me!

31:28.219 --> 31:30.722
My specialty is killing, not saving.

32:06.633 --> 32:09.052
Why do you keep following me?
Got nothing better to do?

32:10.219 --> 32:12.305
I had to get him
from the desert back to Korea,

32:12.388 --> 32:14.599
call an ambulance,
and frame him as delusional!

32:14.682 --> 32:16.601
Why stir up chaos in the modern world?

32:16.684 --> 32:19.103
Why are you suddenly pretending
to be a good guy?

32:20.021 --> 32:22.190
You know, I've been thinking about that.

32:22.273 --> 32:25.485
Ever think I was originally the good guy,
and you were the bad one?

32:27.570 --> 32:30.823
I shall use a very blunt scythe
when I slit your throat.

32:30.907 --> 32:32.033
So one strike won't do.

32:32.116 --> 32:33.201
See?

32:33.284 --> 32:35.495
You and I are no different.

32:36.496 --> 32:39.582
Do you even have time for this?
Don't you need to go see Ki Ka-young?

32:41.209 --> 32:43.628
I guess you're not up for another beating.

32:45.296 --> 32:46.130
What?

32:47.423 --> 32:49.008
Concerned I'll go see her again?

32:51.260 --> 32:53.638
What did you even mean to show her?

32:53.721 --> 32:55.098
What, my cruelty?

32:55.682 --> 32:56.975
Or the wishes she made?

32:57.058 --> 32:59.727
That's why I was punished
for 983 years, no less.

33:01.187 --> 33:02.480
Isn't that enough?

33:07.402 --> 33:08.820
How laughable.

33:10.405 --> 33:12.115
We have lived an eternity,

33:12.699 --> 33:14.575
so that period of less than 1,000 years

33:16.244 --> 33:17.495
was hardly punishment.

33:22.959 --> 33:26.629
I've inspected every element,
and there are no issues with the watch.

33:26.713 --> 33:27.547
Really?

33:30.550 --> 33:32.927
I'm sure the watch hands spun backwards.

33:33.511 --> 33:34.846
Incredibly fast at that.

33:34.929 --> 33:39.600
I've been working here for over ten years,
and I've never had an inquiry like this.

33:39.684 --> 33:42.228
Moreover, it's just impossible, ma'am.

33:55.283 --> 33:56.993
So I really can't let myself in?

34:05.168 --> 34:06.461
What the hell does it say?

34:06.544 --> 34:08.171
It says you shouldn't shake it.

34:08.254 --> 34:10.923
That an ill-tempered genie
might get angry.

34:18.431 --> 34:19.307
TRANSLATE

34:21.392 --> 34:24.187
SHELF LIFE IS INFINITE
FROM DATE OF REMAKING: OCTOBER 24, 1061

34:25.521 --> 34:26.689
So he lied.

34:27.356 --> 34:28.775
If it was the year 1061,

34:28.858 --> 34:31.778
and he said he was confined for 983 years,

34:32.570 --> 34:33.946
he's 20 years short.

34:36.699 --> 34:38.576
It couldn't have been a housing scam.

34:39.786 --> 34:40.828
What is this?

35:09.065 --> 35:10.066
Who are they?

35:11.192 --> 35:13.027
What have they been doing there all day?

35:14.195 --> 35:15.530
Should we bring it up?

35:21.369 --> 35:22.703
Why the intense stares?

35:22.787 --> 35:24.872
What are they looking at all day?

35:27.500 --> 35:30.294
I'm Chauffeur Kim, a former member
of the Reconnaissance Unit.

35:30.378 --> 35:32.839
I sense some intense eyes on us.

35:33.673 --> 35:35.007
Two in the bushes.

35:36.425 --> 35:37.677
Two more in the mansion.

35:38.803 --> 35:39.971
Perhaps more.

35:42.431 --> 35:43.349
Boss,

35:44.308 --> 35:46.477
what kind of life have you led?

35:48.896 --> 35:50.314
I have no other choice.

35:51.607 --> 35:53.734
You can trust me, sir.

36:01.325 --> 36:02.326
Apologies, sir,

36:03.286 --> 36:05.371
but may I ask what you are waiting for?

36:06.998 --> 36:07.832
I'm waiting

36:08.749 --> 36:09.750
for my dad.

36:10.334 --> 36:12.503
This is where I lost my way.

36:14.505 --> 36:16.674
I remember the smell of my dad's car.

36:19.844 --> 36:22.263
My younger brother, Ha-neul. Kim Ha-neul.

36:23.472 --> 36:24.807
He'll be looking for me.

36:27.435 --> 36:28.352
Dad?

36:28.436 --> 36:31.147
Is this short-term memory loss
or something?

36:32.023 --> 36:35.276
What on earth
have you gotten tangled up in, sir?

36:36.527 --> 36:38.821
-That's insane.
-She sure is something.

36:38.905 --> 36:42.325
Can you believe he told me
I can't leave work until she gets here?

36:42.909 --> 36:44.660
I swear the guy's nuts.

36:44.744 --> 36:45.578
This is crazy.

36:45.661 --> 36:47.079
She's here.

36:47.663 --> 36:49.207
Is something wrong?

36:50.958 --> 36:52.543
I honestly can't believe this.

36:52.627 --> 36:53.628
Come with me.

36:58.174 --> 36:59.634
What the hell is going on here?

36:59.717 --> 37:02.094
Why is the money
in Ms. Ki Ka-young's account

37:02.178 --> 37:05.681
being transferred into your account
every day, Ms. Gu?

37:05.765 --> 37:07.058
Are you embezzling?

37:07.642 --> 37:11.145
How could you say such a thing?
It's the first I'm hearing of it too.

37:12.605 --> 37:15.524
For the past two weeks,
there have been transfers of ten million,

37:15.608 --> 37:18.110
then 50 million won every day,
and this is news to you?

37:18.194 --> 37:19.737
This is so damn unfair!

37:20.238 --> 37:23.032
Are you saying I should spend
all my time checking my account?

37:23.658 --> 37:25.952
Huge amounts
were being transferred every day,

37:26.035 --> 37:27.411
and you seriously didn't know?

37:27.495 --> 37:30.539
Our logs show you repeatedly accessed
Ms. Ki Ka-young's information.

37:31.040 --> 37:32.667
How do you explain that?

37:32.750 --> 37:34.835
You asked me to sell her our pension plan.

37:34.919 --> 37:37.964
That's why I looked.
To figure out how to convince her!

37:38.047 --> 37:40.091
You saw the logs, so you'll know.

37:40.174 --> 37:42.260
She came in
to increase her transfer limit.

37:42.343 --> 37:43.970
So why are you doing this to me?

37:44.053 --> 37:47.598
Shouldn't you be speaking
to Ki Ka-young about this, not me?

37:47.682 --> 37:48.891
Why, you…

37:48.975 --> 37:50.601
Given the situation, sir,

37:50.685 --> 37:53.688
the Financial Supervisory Service
must already be investigating--

37:53.771 --> 37:54.897
Shut your mouth!

37:55.481 --> 37:56.524
Of course I know that!

37:57.024 --> 37:57.858
Unbelievable.

37:58.359 --> 38:01.862
Ms. Gu, go meet Ms. Ki Ka-young
before the FSS does,

38:01.946 --> 38:03.948
and find out what has happened here.

38:04.031 --> 38:05.908
You're friends, aren't you? Friends!

38:05.992 --> 38:08.995
All of our jobs are on the line now.

38:10.496 --> 38:11.372
Yes, sir.

38:21.465 --> 38:22.341
I'm back.

38:22.425 --> 38:24.802
Eat up.

38:31.851 --> 38:33.060
Thanks for the book.

38:42.445 --> 38:45.406
HISTORY OF GORYEO

38:55.583 --> 38:56.417
Have you

38:57.835 --> 38:59.253
finally made a decision?

39:05.384 --> 39:08.888
The angels came down
and began slaughtering all genies,

39:09.388 --> 39:11.682
and Ejllael is the one who led the charge.

39:13.517 --> 39:16.562
The war lasted 300 years,

39:17.563 --> 39:19.523
and I lost most of my brothers
as a result.

39:24.653 --> 39:25.821
Lead the way

39:26.405 --> 39:27.740
to the moment I died.

39:38.334 --> 39:39.794
He is displeased

39:40.586 --> 39:44.215
as disasters and droughts
have struck Ifriqiya,

39:45.174 --> 39:46.967
costing countless human lives.

39:47.468 --> 39:49.678
You'd best not provoke them.

39:50.179 --> 39:52.306
Don't overdo it.

39:53.307 --> 39:57.144
Anyway, what is that face you wear?

39:57.728 --> 40:01.816
I chose a face set to be in high demand
across the world for the next millennium.

40:03.192 --> 40:05.069
I'm speaking in their language now too.

40:06.112 --> 40:08.531
My next wish-maker
is on their way from there.

40:45.192 --> 40:47.319
Dogs! Wild hounds!

40:47.820 --> 40:49.155
Run!

40:52.783 --> 40:54.243
A pack of wild hounds!

40:59.457 --> 41:03.127
Dogs! It's a pack of wild hounds!

41:03.210 --> 41:06.130
Just throw that limping boy aside!

41:07.882 --> 41:09.008
No, don't!

41:09.091 --> 41:11.093
You can't!

41:11.719 --> 41:13.053
Don't!

41:16.265 --> 41:17.308
Hunbish!

41:41.540 --> 41:44.210
The time has come for some wishes.

42:04.313 --> 42:07.107
It's Iblis! It's Shaytan!

42:07.608 --> 42:10.611
It's Shaytan! Run!

42:10.694 --> 42:13.614
Where are you going?
Cast the Goryeo bitch aside too!

42:13.697 --> 42:16.617
Run away!

42:19.203 --> 42:21.372
Save me!

42:24.542 --> 42:26.544
Hurry, run!

42:38.055 --> 42:40.099
I am Genie, the lamp spirit.

42:40.849 --> 42:42.560
I shall grant you three wishes.

42:43.310 --> 42:44.228
Make them.

42:45.396 --> 42:47.982
Did you say wishes?

42:49.024 --> 42:51.777
No bringing back the dead.
No traveling to the future.

42:51.860 --> 42:53.404
Anything besides that,

42:53.487 --> 42:54.863
your wish…

42:58.242 --> 42:59.493
is my command.

43:01.579 --> 43:02.955
Are you also

43:03.914 --> 43:05.291
from Goryeo, sir?

43:08.210 --> 43:10.212
If you'd like it that way,
let's say it's so.

43:10.296 --> 43:11.130
Now,

43:11.964 --> 43:13.549
make your first wish.

43:18.429 --> 43:20.222
Please save Hunbish.

43:21.056 --> 43:23.684
Please let him live a long, long life.

43:23.767 --> 43:27.479
Please! He can't just die like this.

43:28.522 --> 43:29.565
That's right.

43:33.027 --> 43:33.986
Come with me

43:35.321 --> 43:36.280
to corruption.

44:04.391 --> 44:05.517
Run!

44:07.353 --> 44:09.104
Do not blame me.

44:09.897 --> 44:13.901
My young master wishes
for someone to live a long life.

44:21.909 --> 44:23.619
And for a long, lengthy life,

44:25.204 --> 44:26.705
a blood sacrifice must be made.

44:30.250 --> 44:31.293
Desert,

44:32.127 --> 44:33.754
be tainted by this blood.

44:36.965 --> 44:38.759
The boy lives,

44:39.510 --> 44:41.303
though the wild hounds will starve.

44:58.237 --> 45:00.739
Now, shall we hear
what your second wish is?

45:04.410 --> 45:06.370
Please make it so that

45:07.955 --> 45:09.456
other children from Goryeo

45:10.332 --> 45:13.085
aren't sold to be animal feed, as I was.

45:16.296 --> 45:17.881
Then I shall cut off the path.

45:19.925 --> 45:21.176
I shall be back soon.

45:38.235 --> 45:41.655
This is probably around 1041 AD.

45:43.115 --> 45:45.492
Are you sure it was the year 1041?

45:46.368 --> 45:47.286
I'm sure.

45:48.036 --> 45:51.498
I remember it as the time when Iblis
was at his height, deceiving humans.

45:52.875 --> 45:55.919
There was an unusually large number
of deaths that year.

45:57.045 --> 45:57.880
Including yours.

46:02.468 --> 46:05.012
You see them, don't you? All those deaths.

46:07.097 --> 46:08.766
All the work of Iblis.

46:35.918 --> 46:36.877
There they are.

46:37.503 --> 46:39.338
Do you see me there with a scythe?

46:41.006 --> 46:43.967
I haven't seen my original face
in a long time.

46:44.760 --> 46:47.054
I'll change it to this face
so it's less jarring.

46:53.936 --> 46:56.647
So your second wish
has also been fulfilled.

46:57.648 --> 46:59.566
The path to Goryeo has been blocked.

46:59.650 --> 47:01.860
Blocking that path
triggered quakes and tsunamis.

47:03.028 --> 47:05.989
With your first wish,
15 of 17 merchants lost their lives,

47:06.073 --> 47:09.535
and due to your second wish,
hundreds of humans died.

47:13.372 --> 47:14.540
That can't be.

47:14.623 --> 47:16.834
I didn't make such wishes.

47:18.794 --> 47:19.711
Please help!

47:23.507 --> 47:24.716
I guess that makes it 16.

47:34.643 --> 47:37.104
Now, only your final wish remains.

47:37.187 --> 47:39.773
Girl from a foreign land, make your wish.

47:42.651 --> 47:46.488
This is not what I wanted.

47:48.365 --> 47:49.616
What do I do now?

47:50.158 --> 47:53.203
I made the wrong kinds of wishes.

47:55.330 --> 47:56.290
How foolish.

47:57.499 --> 47:59.793
There's no such thing as the right wish.

48:00.419 --> 48:02.963
To gain something,
something else must be lost.

48:03.463 --> 48:06.133
For someone to live, another must die.

48:07.217 --> 48:08.135
Sade!

48:34.494 --> 48:37.789
You may say such things, but your
final wish will be "please save me."

48:39.124 --> 48:39.958
So make your wish.

48:48.342 --> 48:49.384
No.

48:51.136 --> 48:52.554
I accept

48:53.847 --> 48:55.140
whatever punishment.

48:56.475 --> 48:57.976
So please,

48:58.602 --> 48:59.770
make sure…

49:02.105 --> 49:04.149
we are punished.

49:05.233 --> 49:08.111
You and I both.

49:11.406 --> 49:12.366
What?

49:12.449 --> 49:14.826
It's only fair.

49:15.911 --> 49:17.079
This

49:18.080 --> 49:20.290
is my final wish.

49:31.051 --> 49:32.469
You lowly thing. You dare…

49:34.763 --> 49:37.474
You petty human,
molded from mere clay. You dare?

49:43.647 --> 49:44.648
Behold.

49:44.731 --> 49:47.526
His creations
are truly righteous and beautiful.

49:47.609 --> 49:48.944
You have lost, Iblis.

49:49.945 --> 49:51.571
You remember his words, don't you?

49:52.072 --> 49:54.866
If you happen to meet
even one pure human, you will forever…

49:54.950 --> 49:56.284
-Just wait.
-No, forever!

49:56.368 --> 49:57.953
Wait, just wait!

50:01.123 --> 50:02.374
Righteous?

50:04.042 --> 50:05.335
I'm not sure.

50:07.254 --> 50:08.171
Because really,

50:08.255 --> 50:10.465
there's room for interpretation here.

50:11.967 --> 50:14.636
So would you put in
a good word for me, Brother?

50:19.766 --> 50:20.809
Cut the crap.

50:28.775 --> 50:30.152
Is this really the end?

50:31.236 --> 50:32.070
Really?

50:33.780 --> 50:34.740
Hey, come back.

50:35.323 --> 50:36.158
Ejllael.

50:36.783 --> 50:37.951
Get back down here!

50:47.085 --> 50:48.462
You lowly clay. You dare…

50:48.962 --> 50:51.256
You lowly being, molded on a Friday.

50:51.339 --> 50:53.967
Mere human who lives
for less than 100 years. You dare!

52:03.745 --> 52:04.579
Do you see?

52:04.663 --> 52:06.832
Your death was so tragic.

52:08.250 --> 52:10.085
Iblis is an evil bastard

52:10.168 --> 52:12.796
who twisted every wish you made,
no matter what it was,

52:12.879 --> 52:14.172
to lead you to corruption.

52:30.272 --> 52:31.106
It wasn't…

52:33.108 --> 52:34.192
rage.

52:37.154 --> 52:39.197
When I saw him in the lamp,

52:39.781 --> 52:41.449
it definitely looked like rage.

52:42.409 --> 52:43.326
But this…

52:45.996 --> 52:46.830
This face…

52:50.375 --> 52:51.668
is undeniably

52:53.003 --> 52:54.004
true sorrow.

53:39.674 --> 53:40.634
How laughable.

53:43.178 --> 53:46.848
We have lived an eternity,
so that period of less than 1,000 years

53:46.932 --> 53:48.183
was hardly punishment.

57:36.244 --> 57:41.249
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
